users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"open_issues":343,"closed_issues":2335,"state":"open","created_at":"2026-04-13T15:59:35Z","updated_at":"2026-10-22T06:28:22Z","due_on":null,"closed_at":null},"comments":2,"created_at":"2026-08-07T10:37:09Z","updated_at":"2026-10-09T14:41:50Z","closed_at":"2026-10-09T14:41:50Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- reproducible in: 4.7.1\n- not reproducible in: 4.5, 4.6.3\n\nI bisected the issue to 05c915566c869aa29275a48a206bdc843436cb8f, from PR #105791.\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.7.1.stable.mono - Linux Mint 22.2 (Zara) on X11 - X11 display driver, Multi-window, 1 monitor - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated AMD Radeon RX 570 Series (RADV POLARIS10)\n\n### Issue description\n\nThe editor's 3d viewport camera exhibits incorrect panning behaviour, snapping back to previous positions even when it clearly shouldn't, or at the very least without the user intending it to.\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b50e0f46-90ff-47fa-972b-5aa4ef1dac31\n\nThis behaviour is extremely jarring and makes any kind of usage of the 3d viewport a fight against the editor. The behaviour was not present in versions of Godot before 4.7, so users familiar with the old panning behaviour are likely to constantly stumble onto this.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. open a 3d editor viewport\n2. hold the middle mouse button\n3. while holding the middle mouse button, move the mouse around to pan\n4. stop moving the mouse\n5. without moving the mouse even a single pixel, release the middle mouse button\n6. without moving the mouse even a single pixel, press and hold the right mouse button\n7. observe that the camera has now incorrectly snapped back to the position before the middle-mouse pan, and the right mouse button pan is now completely ignored by the editor and won't move the camera at all\n\nThese steps are shown performed in the video within the issue description.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nNone. This issue occurs in all projects as far as I can tell, even in newly-created blank 3d projects.","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122185/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122185/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null}